<title>CHINA: Central China province reaps bumper early rice.</title>
<headline>Central China province reaps bumper early rice.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-09-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's central Jiangxi province harvested the second largest early rice yield in its history this year, the Farmers' Daily said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The bumper harvest came after earlier worries that crops could be badly affected after some of the worst floods in a century hit central and southern China in July and August.</p>
<p>Jiangxi province had harvested 6.69 million tonnes of early rice output this year, 1.24 million tonnes more than in 1995, the newspaper said. It gave no details of the provinces biggest summer rice output.</p>
</text>
